    {
      "id": "p0139-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "It's explained throughout Underta/e's story that when monsters die, they turn into dust. This simple fact became a little more complicated during the localization process, because there are multiple words in Japanese that mean \"dust'', each with its slightly different nuances. The localization team narrowed the choices down to three:",
        "raw": "It's explained throughout Underta/e's story that when monsters die, they\nturn into dust. This simple fact became a little more complicated during the\nlocalization process, because there are multiple words in Japanese that mean\n\"dust'', each with its slightly different nuances. The localization team narrowed\nthe choices down to three:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08329373,
          0.25775,
          0.69671758,
          0.34448571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0812467,
          0.25703571,
          0.70543794,
          0.34555714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19,
          20
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Undertale 的故事多次说明，怪物死后会化为尘埃。这个简单的事实，到了本地化时却稍微复杂了一点：日语中有好几个表示“dust”的词，细微含义各不相同。团队最后把候选词缩小到三个：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
